---
title: "Code Highlight"
description: "Code examples with syntax highlighting, done at build time."
tags: [typography, css]
usage: |
  Write a fenced code block in Markdown with a language name, for example
  ` ```php `, inside a `<code-highlight>` element. The site build highlights it
  with Prism, so no JavaScript runs in the browser.
accessibility: |
  - Make sure the highlighting colors keep enough contrast with the background.
  - Long lines scroll horizontally; keep examples short so they can be read
    without scrolling where possible.
---

<code-highlight>
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="./styles.css"
    media="screen"
  >
  {{ include "./_example.md" |> md }}
</code-highlight>
